        "@id": "https://www.phtheatre.org/stec_event/stand-2024-17/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "STAND: APÄTRIDA (Stateless)"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<strong>November 16, 2024</strong>\r\n<strong>7:30 PM – 9:00 PM</strong>\r\n\r\nThrough this compelling performance, Pablo Zacarías shares his unique perspective on his family’s narrative of intergenerational displacement and the profound quest for identity and belonging through songs, stories, and jokes.\r\n\r\nPablo is a human rights advocate and pioneer in Spanish-language stand-up in BC. He headlined the first Latinx comedy show at the Vancouver Playhouse. He became the first Vancouver-based Latinx comedian to perform solo at venues like Performance Works and Presentation House Theatre."
      }
    ],
